  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "What is the value of ${\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{4{log}_{4}\u2061x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x?$",
  "worked_solution": "Let $u={log}_{4}\u2061x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}\u20614}\\,\u27f9\\,\\operatorname{ln}\u20614\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{4{log}_{4}\u2061x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =4{\\int }_{1}^{4}{log}_{4}\u2061x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{1}u\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}\u20614\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}\u20614{\\int }_{0}^{1}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}\u20614\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}\u20614\\cdot (1-0) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}\u20614 \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}\u20612\\end{aligned}\n$$",
